  "verbalization": "NRF2 activator Geopyxin F is shown to have a direct target of SNU-387, which is a compound that acts as a target for multiple downstream pathways, including those involving the prostate. The evidence suggests that SNU-387 is a target of both 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one and Licochalcone D, both of which are known to interact with prostate cells. This indicates that Geopyxin F may influence prostate cell function through the activation of these pathways, potentially leading to cellular responses that are relevant to prostate health or disease. The integration of these findings suggests a possible role for Geopyxin F in modulating prostate cell activity via the targeting of these compounds, highlighting a complex network of interactions that may underlie its effects on prostate cells.",
